"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[5111],{45111:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"ipoteka-sentyabr-2026-rekord-vydachi","locale":"en","title":"Banks issue 608.5 billion rubles of September mortgages before family-program tightening","description":"Banks issued 123.8 thousand mortgages worth 608.5 billion rubles in September 2026 before the family mortgage program tightened. What followed earlier surges.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Russian banks issued 123.8 thousand mortgages worth 608.5 billion rubles in September 2026. The number of contracts rose by 45% from August and their value by 63%. This was the highest amount since December 2025, when issuance reached 802.9 billion rubles. Family mortgages accounted for most of it. VTB mortgage-lending head Sergei Babin estimates their September issuance at about 385 billion rubles, 2 times August\'s level."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Households hurried because terms were changing. From October 1, 2026, family mortgage rates depend on the number of children and the region; previously everyone paid 6%. A family with 1 child now pays 10% in the regions and 12% in Moscow, St Petersburg and their surrounding regions; with 2 children, the rates are 8% and 10%. Contracts signed through September 30 retain the old terms. On the final day, Sberbank issued 7.4 thousand family mortgages worth 46.6 billion rubles, a program record for 1 day."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"It resembles a shop before an announced price increase: customers stock up and fewer return in the following weeks. Some September transactions would have happened anyway, just later. Such a rush before a rule change is called a deadline effect. Mortgages have already shown it 2 times in 2026. In January 2026, before a February 1 ban on more than 1 subsidized mortgage per family, issuance reached about 420 billion rubles. February then produced 290.3 billion, 31% less. In June, when tightening was expected from July 1, issuance rose by 48% from May. On June 29, the Finance Ministry postponed the changes until October, but July issuance still fell by 25%."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Other lending did not increase in September. In total, households took out 3.14 million loans worth 1.33 trillion rubles in September 2026, 20.8% more than in August. Cash-loan issuance was roughly unchanged at 515.4 billion rubles, while car loans fell by 2%. With the Bank of Russia\'s key rate at 14%, ordinary credit is expensive and households have not borrowed more of it."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"Consider a regional family with 1 child. A 6 million ruble loan over 30 years at 6% costs about 36 thousand rubles a month. At 10%, the same loan costs about 52.7 thousand rubles during the first 15 years. A rate of up to 6% remains available for such a family in 2 cases: a child has a disability or the down payment is at least 50% of the home\'s price."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"October issuance data will appear in early November. A sharp fall would mean September borrowed demand from later months, as happened in February and July. If issuance holds up, families are willing to borrow at 10–12%. A family with 1 child that missed the deadline now faces a rate 4–6 percentage points above the old one. The family mortgage rate is set by the program, so a Bank of Russia key-rate cut will not reduce it. Postponing a purchase means continuing to pay rent, while whether housing prices will fall remains unknown."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did mortgage issuance rise in September 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"From October 1, 2026, family mortgage rates for households with 1 or 2 children rose from 6% to 8–12%, so families rushed to sign on the old terms. Banks issued mortgages worth 608.5 billion rubles in September, 63% more than in August."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What happened after previous family mortgage tightenings?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Issuance fell. In February 2026, after January\'s surge, mortgages totaled 290.3 billion rubles, 31% less than in January. July issuance fell by 25% after June\'s growth, even though the changes were postponed and terms remained unchanged."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Will a family mortgage signed in September retain its 6% rate?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Yes. The new terms apply only to contracts concluded from October 1, 2026. Those signing through September 30 continue paying the previous rate."}],"sources":[{"label":"Mortgage issuance jumps before a key state program tightens","url":"https://thebell.io/vydachi-ipoteki-podskochili-pered-uzhestocheniem-klyuchevoy-gosprogrammy"},{"label":"Russian mortgage issuance sets a September record","url":"https://realty.rbc.ru/news/6ac352bc89d57af63b2fbdf8"},{"label":"Family mortgages in September 2026: record issuance before reform","url":"https://www.sravni.ru/text/semeynaya-ipoteka-rekord-sentyabr-2026/"},{"label":"December 2025 family mortgage issuance reaches a 1.5-year high","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/vyidachi-semejnoj-ipoteki-v-dekabre-2025-goda-dostigli-maksimuma-za-15-goda-69195191/"},{"label":"February mortgage issuance drops by a third after family-program tightening","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/03/06/vidacha-ipoteki-v-fevrale-ruhnula-na-tret-posle-uzhestocheniya-uslovii-dlya-semeinih-rossiyan-a189017"},{"label":"Central bank: July mortgage issuance falls to 363 billion as the market cools after June\'s surge","url":"https://finuslugi.ru/navigator/news/novosti_bankovskoj_otrasli/tsb-vydachi-ipoteki-upali-do-363-mlrd-v-iyule-rynok-ostyl-posle-iyunskogo-vspleska"},{"label":"Finance Ministry announces retention of current Family Mortgage terms","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/minfin-perenes-izmeneniya-semejnoj-ipoteki-do-oktyabrya-69215609/"},{"label":"The Bank of Russia kept the key rate at 14%","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/press/keypr/"}],"sourceBodySha256":"69a454caaee0d4b2b465e488d24b624bdcc43ee4fb07418714c00cd6de309533"}')}}]);